# Checkwright core-file manifest — gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-core-files.
# One repo-relative path per line, or a `kit:<basename>` token deriving one path
# per kit root (`#` comments, blank lines ignored). The gate
# is red when a listed path is missing from the worktree or untracked. Retiring
# a surface deliberately means deleting its line in the same commit that removes
# the file — that manifest edit is the diff-visible intentional-removal valve.

# Iteration state machine + governance charter.
TASK-QUEUE.md
# Public direction: the generated projection of the queue's curated [roadmap:] tags.
ROADMAP.md
.workflow/WORKFLOW-STATE.txt
README.md
CLAUDE.md

# Public contribution surface: guide + GitHub-rendered issue/PR templates.
CONTRIBUTING.md
# Conduct surface: GitHub renders it from this root basename.
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
# Disclosure route: the Security tab renders it from this root basename.
SECURITY.md
# Release runbook: governed repo-meta, the repeatable release procedure.
RELEASING.md
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/gate-defect.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/install-failure.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/doc-problem.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/adoption-report.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml
.github/pull_request_template.md

# CI backstop: the workflow template + this repo's filled instance (§ci-backstop).
gate-sdk/templates/gates-workflow.yml
.github/workflows/gates.yml

# Live-site monitoring (not a gate): the scheduled deployment probe.
.github/workflows/site-health.yml

# The installer package's publish channel (RELEASING.md §The procedure step 5).
.github/workflows/publish.yml

# The installer's own entry points (CLAUDE.md §Housekeeping).
installer/package.json
installer/bin/checkwright.sh

# Gate registry + graph rule content + the checked pre-commit/graph projections.
scripts/gates.list
scripts/gate-sdk-config.sh
scripts/graph-vocab.sh
scripts/identity.conf
scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit
docs/check-graph.html

# Derived per kit root: each kit's canonical contract and its entry-point README.
# These expand to one path per kit root, so kit twelve is covered on the commit
# that creates it — no line here to remember.
kit:SPEC.md
kit:README.md
# Hand-held: a single-kit deliverable with no per-kit counterpart, so no kit:
# token can express it (kit:DOCTRINE.md would demand it of all eleven roots).
doctrine-kit/DOCTRINE.md

# Held-constant validate baseline + committed per-run evidence manifest.
.workflow/validate-baseline.txt
.workflow/validate-evidence.txt
